            <p>Kant's project was to ground morality in pure reason, independent of human nature or consequences. Whether he succeeded is a question you will keep encountering in the rest of the course. Mill, whom we read next, will argue that Kant's whole enterprise is misguided, and that the right foundation for ethics is exactly what Kant ruled out: consequences, and specifically human happiness.</p>
